==Strategy==
While one might assume this stage works similarly to [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 50|Heavenly Tower's Floor 50]], the addition of two enemies makes things complicated. Using [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] becomes much less effective due to the presence of Metal Snaches and Pure Gold R.Osts, which absorb his attacks. The Metal Snaches, particularly, have over 160 HP, allowing them to tank absurd amounts of damage without [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]]. That said, these peons provide the perfect platform to snipe Master Uril from a safe distance. The most effective strategy for beating this stage revolves around abusing Master Uril's low standing range to snipe him with piercing units like [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Golfer Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]] while keeping him at bay using [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr.]]. By setting up [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell Cat]] and in such a way that Jagando attacks beyond the Metal Snaches, you can stall out Master Uril and build yourself a stack of units to damage him over time. The Pure Gold R.Ost waves will stand no chance against the giant stack of units you inevitably build up as long as you keep sending out Green Shell Cats and other meatshields to fill in the gaps, letting you brute-force their HP. Even with this, it is still generally recommended to bring at least one unit with the [[Critical Hit]] ability to handle the cleanup.

Gold Hippoe and Golden Doges pose no threat whatsoever, and serve as a steady source of income. You are not likely to run low on cash throughout most of this stage, unless you are running an extremely expensive loadout.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Thanks to his [[Explosion]] Talent giving him forward piercing range, Awakened Bahamut Cat can repeatedly target Metal Snaches to continuously damage Master Uril, occasionally knocking him back.
*Talented [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]]: Unlocking his [[Immune to Surge]] and [[Mini-Wave]] Talents, Li'l King Dragon can steadily chip away at both Master Uril and Pure Gold R.Osts.
*Talented [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]]: With his Surge Attack Talent, Dancer Cat is capable of sniping Master Uril from a relatively safe distance. Although his Surge Attacks can be somewhat inconsistent, they still do significant damage. Dancer Cat tends to eat up your wallet, so Rich Cat is recommended if you plan on using him. He is also very fragile, and won't survive a single attack from Master Uril.
*[[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]]: With his high range, he can reliably damage Gold Hippoes while also sniping Master Uril with his Long Distance attacks. Thanks to his [[Massive Damage]] VS Traitless enemies, his performance against the boss is among the highest of all non-Uber units.
*[[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Elder Beast Naala/Awakened Naala]]: Deals sizeable damage to Master Uril regardless of distance, its Surge Immunity allows it to take advantage of both of its knockbacks. This makes Naala an incredibly decent Long Distance attacker if you own them.
*[[Bowler Cat (Rare Cat)|Bowler Cat]]: When stacked on the Metal peons, Bowler Cat does amazingly well on this stage. His Mini-Waves let him [[Slow]] Uril from afar, giving time to build up attackers like Hitman Cat.
*[[Brainwashed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Flying Cat]]: Can be used as a substitute for Bowler Cat: with lower HP, range, Mini-Wave level, and a far higher cost. In exchange, they have a better attack rate, quicker recharge, and higher DPS due to their Massive Damage against Traitless. Beware, as while they have [[Immune to Surge|Surge Immunity]], they lack [[Immune to Curse|Curse Immunity]], which means they cannot bounce back from a Uril attack like Bowler Cat can.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]: Despite the abundance of Metal enemies in this stage. Cyberpunk can still be used to Slow Master Uril in order to prevent him from catching up to your front lines. Keep in mind, he is somewhat inconsistent.
*[[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]]: Equipped with high Knockback, high range, and a relatively decent Critical Hit odds (considering his fast attack speed), he is well-suited to handle every Metal enemy in this stage. However, due to his 6% Critical Hit chance, you may experience long streaks without triggering his ability even once. Only send him out during the Pure Gold R.Ost waves to prevent him from unnecessarily killing Metal Snaches.
*[[Volley Cat (Rare Cat)|Curry Cat]]: His Long Distance attacks combined with Critical Hit make him a decent counter to Pure Gold R.Ost. Beware, his Critical Hit chance is only 8%, giving him a similar problem to Cat Researcher.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Kubiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|E. Kubilan Pasalan]]: If the sheer abundance of Metal enemies begins to overrun you, Kubilan can instantly clear the field with his guaranteed Level 8 Critical [[Wave Attack]]s. Beware, his long cooldown prevents him from being re-deployed ever again after use. He should be reserved as a last-ditch, hail-mary option in case of emergencies. Do not deploy him otherwise.
*[[Izanami of Dusk (Legend Rare Cat)|Izanami of Eventide]]/[[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|Valiant D'arktanyan]]: Very good for clearing out Golden Doge and Gold Hippoe, but is mostly used here for Master Uril because of their huge damage vs Traitless. You can use the Metals as a platform to snipe the boss without letting him get surge attacks off.
*[[Gravi (Uber Rare Cat)|Gravolodon]]: Boasting a powerful [[Wave Attack]], a large HP pool, and a defense combo with [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell Cat]], Gravolodon is the perfect assistant for stacking strategies that do not plan to kill the metal snaches until Uril is dead. Due to its low range, however, it will prove actively detrimental in strategies that use Critical Hits during the fight.
*[[Dark Mitama (Uber Rare Cat)|Dark Mitama]]/[[Miko Mitama (Uber Rare Cat)|Mitama the Oracle]]: Her long distance, somewhat high uptime slow against Traitless allows her to slow Uril with Metal Snaches as a stepping stone. She also can Weaken the Gold Hippoe as well as Uril himself which could be the difference between whether the stack survives a hit. In the case for her Uberfest version, it works for Pure Gold R.Ost instead of the Traitless enemies.

